  "body": {
    "id": "prop:lower-class-sr-inclusion",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "The fixed exponent-two class is contained in the Sanjaroonpouri--Ramazi observational class:\n\\[\n \\mathcal M_\\star\\subseteq\\mathcal M_{\\mathrm{SR}}.\n\\]",
    "free_symbols": [
      "Mstar",
      "SRClass"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:fourier-model",
      "def:lower-class",
      "def:sr-published-class"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Take \\(P_X\\in\\mathcal M_\\star\\).  By \\(\\mathrm{def:lower\\text{-}class}\\), \\(P_X\\in\\mathcal M\\), and \\(\\mathrm{def:fourier\\text{-}model}\\) supplies \\(X=AH+G_\\Gamma\\) with \\(H\\perp G_\\Gamma\\), \\(1\\le k\\le p\\), mutually independent nonconstant source coordinates, \\(\\operatorname{Var}(H_j)=1\\), \\(\\operatorname{rank}(A)=k\\), lexicographically sorted columns, and no nondegenerate Gaussian convolution divisor for any \\(H_j\\).  Independence and the unit variances give \\(\\operatorname{Cov}(H)=I_k\\).  A nonconstant Gaussian variable has a nondegenerate Gaussian convolution divisor (split its positive variance into two positive summands), so Gaussian indecomposability also implies that every \\(H_j\\) is non-Gaussian.  Every defining condition of \\(\\mathrm{def:sr\\text{-}published\\text{-}class}\\) follows, proving \\(P_X\\in\\mathcal M_{\\mathrm{SR}}\\).",
